googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/54/305154/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I2d0c98760494e2f4657ee35b6f155690939d2d18" commit="1c1ca7211da42b22b6a623b0089276bc2d871e85" commit_message="skylake: add support for verstage  The right files just need to be added to the verstage build. Do that so a stand alone verstage builds and links.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and booted glados.  Change-Id: I2d0c98760494e2f4657ee35b6f155690939d2d18 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304648 Reviewed-by: Leroy P Leahy &lt;leroy.p.leahy@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="304648" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/48/304648/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Id2b05548e4e10cd12002286913f2228b84802e63" commit="faba1772974357c10ab38c41ead63097fc7c9cdd" commit_message="glados: add chromeos.c to verstage  In order to build stand alone verstage the chromeos.c file needs to be part of the verstage target.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and booted glados.  Change-Id: Id2b05548e4e10cd12002286913f2228b84802e63 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304649 Reviewed-by: Leroy P Leahy &lt;leroy.p.leahy@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="304649" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/49/304649/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I2b3e088326d5a965ad90806a7950b9f401ed57de" commit="c463e5f7d8312dfd52bae4a48bd75999b95fe6db" commit_message="soc/intel/common: use prog_locate() for finding fsp.bin  The current method was only taking the cbfs path. Because of this fsp.bin was never being utilized from the RW slots. Using prog_locate() now provides both the cbfs and vboot locate methods for free.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and booted glados.  Change-Id: I2b3e088326d5a965ad90806a7950b9f401ed57de Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304810 Tested-by: Leroy P Leahy &lt;leroy.p.leahy@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Leroy P Leahy &lt;leroy.p.leahy@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="304810" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/10/304810/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia0fae7ea4ec7f96dcced4ba934a371db324f2f61" commit="9a16ba7408888b63f86dcdcc3f6021615bb59b25" commit_message="add high resolution image options and decision logic  Boot-splash script currently determines screen resolution by running frecon and then runs it again with a list of images in command line. This change adds an option in frecon to pass two lists of images and frecon will make a decision which one to use based on screen resoltion. Therefore the script will not have run frecon to discover resolution and there will be one mode switch less at boot time which should make it faster.  BUG=chromium:541780 TEST=run bootperf  Change-Id: Ia0fae7ea4ec7f96dcced4ba934a371db324f2f61 Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305054 Reviewed-by: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305054" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/frecon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/frecon" ref="refs/changes/54/305054/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Icc16d440c60fd39b3432d78ed4ad5d121edc84af" commit="15f6d49e4dfb52a6f72242619fad55a9bce230ac" commit_message="boot-splash: let frecon decide between normal and hires boot animation  Instead of running frecon twice and deciding which set of PNG files to use, pass both sets of files when starting frecon and let it decide which set to use. This saves us from running frecon twice and two mode switches.  BUG=chromium:541780 TEST=run bootperf CQ-DEPEND=CL:305054  Change-Id: Icc16d440c60fd39b3432d78ed4ad5d121edc84af Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304937 Reviewed-by: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304937" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/37/304937/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I21d6a7a4179a4fcdc98ecae92eecab2829ba48f3" commit="33201512db7483b5ae186d7bc70f34f1efb451c3" commit_message="Set up report metadata regardless of whether version is available.  The Report metadata is needed in the Report stage in order to calculate the failure message, so set it up.  BUG=chromium:542325 TEST=CQ run in --debug mode.  Change-Id: I21d6a7a4179a4fcdc98ecae92eecab2829ba48f3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305240 Commit-Ready: David James &lt;davidjames@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David James &lt;davidjames@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305240" owner_email="davidjames@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/40/305240/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4e21151d03d1050999ea2045b2be4b99886ff15c" commit="32577e84c4a81de6ebda0e24d0a8bc812711d048" commit_message="cr50: upgrade to the latest FPGA image (20151012_041715@75660)  This patch updates the EC codebase to match the suggested USB build. The spiflash utility must come from the same tarball.  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=as follows:      - programmed the FPGA, it now reports the following when reset:       boot_rom 20151012_041715@75660     - booted the new image using the latest spiflash version. Note       that the bootrom now reports the FPGA image it comes from     - disconnected the FPGA upgrade port, rebooted the device, entered       on the device console:        &gt; spstp off        &gt; spste      run on the workstation:        $ examples/spiraw.py -l 10 -f 800000        FT232H Future Technology Devices International, Ltd initialized at 857142 hertz      and observe on the DUT console:        Processed 10 frames rx count 11604, tx count 5512, tx_empty 10, max rx batch 11        &gt;  Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I4e21151d03d1050999ea2045b2be4b99886ff15c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/305260 Commit-Ready: Marius Schilder &lt;mschilder@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Marius Schilder &lt;mschilder@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="305260" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/60/305260/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie0ea13001a588c5e2d743e5eb55f6cf840039155" commit="f8d4f13aa1d95f7c9e19da9eb23aa6c491f3c643" commit_message="project-moblab: Remove USB-Ethernet requirement.  Reorganized moblab-network-bridge-init to still properly set up the moblab network bridge and make the USB Ethernet optional. This ensures that the devserver is always reachable at 192.168.231.1  BUG=None. TEST=MobLab initialization is successful with or without the usb ethernet adaptor.  Change-Id: Ie0ea13001a588c5e2d743e5eb55f6cf840039155 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304603 Commit-Ready: Gilad Arnold &lt;garnold@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Gilad Arnold &lt;garnold@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="304603" owner_email="sbasi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/03/304603/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic4f90624f8ad25144a4bb9b6ba4f2f0731e96fe9" commit="7c436f4a59bba28a66307d89c363d876ececb1ff" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: reduce brk randomization range to 32MB  On ARM64 64-bit processes, the randomized layout of the process virtual address space is broken as we can randomily end up with the bottom of the heap (start_brk) very close to the close to the top of the stack (less than 8MB) or even the brk range above the stack.  Currently for a 64-bit process with 39 bits of VA, (ie STACK_TOP/TASK_SIZE64 at 0x8000000000) we are setting STACK_RND_MASK to 0x3ffff * PAGE_SIZE (ie a 1GB VA range). In fs/binfmt_elf.c, randomize_stack_top() puts our &quot;real&quot; stack top between 0 and 1GB (STACK_RND_MASK) below STACK_TOP. In arch/arm64/mm/mmap.c, MIN_GAP is defined by : (SZ_128M + ((STACK_RND_MASK &lt;&lt; PAGE_SHIFT) + 1)) and mmap_base is &quot;STACK_TOP - gap - mmap_rnd()&quot; (with mmap_rnd() being randomly decided in a 1GB range defined by STACK_RND_MASK) So between the &quot;real&quot; mmap_base and the &quot;real&quot; stack top we have between 128MB and 2176 MB ( 2 x 1GB aka STACK_RND_MASK + 128 MB). Now, arch_randomize_brk() move the bottom of brk within this space by 0 to 1GB (STACK_RND_MASK). So worst case, start_brk is 896 MB above the real top of the stack.  Reduce the BRK randomization range from 1GB to 32MB (25 bits) as used on x86 platforms.  Signed-off-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=b:24042586 TEST=Spawn 180K processes with a Java virtual machine, trace the brk and the stack addresses for each process and compute the gap between them, see a linear distribution between 100MB and 2.1GB. Used to fail with less than 100 processes before as the JVM stack initialization was colliding in the heap.  Change-Id: Ic4f90624f8ad25144a4bb9b6ba4f2f0731e96fe9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304889 Commit-Ready: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kees Cook &lt;keescook@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304889" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/89/304889/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I421d5d9c659ca654494e10cb37456de6fdd9752d" commit="f2ae55ad5d9a4036c48b49c580ab148f09b0f022" commit_message="Brillo Tier 1 PTS: Initial Script.  Here is the starting point for the Brillo Tier 1 PTS.  Currently it does the following:  * Connects to a MobLab instance. * Adds the ADB Host to the MobLab host list. * Stages an update payload (not yet used). * Launches the Brillo PTS Sequence.  Added the Brillo PTS Sequence. Currently is just runs the whitelisted Gtests twice.  Updated sequences to support using the local control file and not the template.  BUG=b:24774860 TEST=Ran against a local moblab, payload is staged and whitelisted Gtests run twice.  Change-Id: I421d5d9c659ca654494e10cb37456de6fdd9752d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304792 Commit-Ready: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304792" owner_email="sbasi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/92/304792/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7541.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>